[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, inside the [38;5;153m<main>[39m element:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
    Example task
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's the browser's built-in checkbox, so the on/off state works without any JavaScript. Because it's wrapped in a
  [38;5;153m<label>[39m, clicking the text also toggles it, and it works with the keyboard and screen readers. I haven't opened it in
  a browser, and I haven't committed it.

  Change "Example task" to whatever item you want. To add more items, copy the [38;5;153m<label>[39m block.

  Two optional extras: the state resets when the page reloads, and checked items aren't crossed out. I can add saving or
  strike-through styling if you want either.

